    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="0185" n="1019" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1019"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/8190c</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Diplomatic Representatives in Certain Countries
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d122-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-25T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 25, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Confer with Allied colleagues before recommending changes in enemy trading list.
                    If agreement results from conference, report decision and reasons. If
                    disagreement results, send your opinion and variant opinions of colleagues with
                    reasons. In each case give <pb facs="0186" n="1020" xml:id="pg1020"/>
                    nationality and residence of person or association recommended for addition or
                    removal from list. Repeat to consuls.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d122-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d122-f1-content">
                <p>Argentina, Bolivia, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Costa Rica, Cuba, Dominican
                    Republic, Ecuador, Guatemala, Haiti, Honduras, Mexico, Nicaragua, Panama,
                    Paraguay, and Peru.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
